From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:10:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: Describe Tensor G4 secure PMU

Stock zumapro.dtsi names the PMU samsung,gs101-pmu, with the secure
write transport implemented in Google's exynos-pmu-if.c. The existing
zuma data provides that transport without attaching gs101 CPU hooks
or register tables. Describe G4 with a zuma fallback so no new driver
match is needed.

This does not add CPU hooks, a register access table, power-domain
policy or the unresolved PCIe masked-update callback. No board node
is added.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/zumapro/+/8831630eee2ad095b85ed452944e6353940966a5/dts/zumapro.dtsi#503
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/soc/google/exynos-pmu-if.c
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
index 14caf5bdc..d594982f2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@ properties:
       - enum:
           - google,gs101-pmu
           - google,zuma-pmu
+      - items:
+          - const: google,zumapro-pmu
+          - const: google,zuma-pmu
       - items:
           - enum:
               - samsung,exynos3250-pmu
